The data exists in the database. The RLS policies look correct. The issue is that the absences_manager policy has WITH CHECK: null for INSERT - this means the insert policy has no WITH CHECK clause, which in Supabase means it defaults to the USING clause. But wait, for ALL policies, the USING clause applies to SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE and the WITH CHECK applies to INSERT/UPDATE. If WITH CHECK is null for an ALL policy, it should inherit the USING clause for inserts.

