This is a nested select joining to reps. The reps table has its own RLS. The reps_read policy says auth.uid() IS NOT NULL which means any authenticated user can read reps. So the join should work.

Actually, I think the problem might be something simpler - the with_check is null for the ALL policy. In PostgreSQL RLS, when you create a policy with FOR ALL and only specify USING, the WITH CHECK for INSERT defaults to the USING expression. So inserts should work with current_user_role() = 'manager'.

